<p>I think that's an interpretation issue. It can just as easily be said that this skip is an emergent phenomenon produced by the interaction of minds that lent themselves to discovery and, later, formalized science. Perhaps it isn't that the skip is an attempt to explain humanity's curiosity and drive for discovery and innovation, but that it's our collective curiosity and drive for discovery and innovation that produce this phenomenon via means we don't yet understand (and as the article seems to imply - that IT itself doesn't yet understand either). +1</p>

