														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1908675">
									

<p>Careful. You can't always please everybody. Sometimes you'll get feedback like this that calls you out on a (frankly, perfectly legitimate) problem with the core idea of your skip. In these situations, sometimes the only way to correct the problem is to abandon the skip and start over. I wouldn't recommend this unless you already have a clear, solid idea for how to fix it.</p>
<p>+40 is honestly pretty good. If there were lots of people all telling you the idea is unworkable, then yeah, I'd say considering abandoning the skip. But I don't think that's the situation you're in with this skip.</p>
<p>I don't have a problem with skips that redefine the basic precepts of the human condition in the mainlist, as long as they're done well. (If it weren't for the &quot;no canon/multi-canon&quot; rule, I'd probably have more of a problem with it.)</p>

